{
  "info": {
    "name": "Notifications Function",
    "description": "Notifications endpoints (phase 7) and the order outcome that fills them.\n\nBase URL: `{{notificationsBaseUrl}}` (defaults to the Aspire launch profile, `http://localhost:5104`). Notifications is an **Azure Function** (isolated worker): a Service Bus trigger consumes `OrderConfirmed` / `OrderRejected`, stores the notification and e-mails it; this HTTP trigger is what the panel reads. Every error response is RFC 9457 `application/problem+json`.\n\nThe **Order flow (end to end)** folder needs Ordering and Catalog running as well (`{{orderingBaseUrl}}`): it places an order and polls until the notification of its outcome appears, which is the whole choreography plus one more hop (Ordering → Service Bus → Inventory → Service Bus → Ordering → Service Bus → Notifications).\n\nE-mails are captured by **Mailpit**, the mail catcher the AppHost starts: open `http://localhost:8025` to read them. `emailStatus` on each row says what happened to that second channel (`Pending`, `Skipped`, `Sent`, `Failed`); the notification is stored either way, which is why a mail server being down never loses one.\n\n**Sign in first.** Every service validates the JWT the Gateway issues, so the collection starts by calling `{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/auth/token` and sends the token as a bearer token on every request. Demo accounts (password `demo`): `bar` and `market` (role `PointOfSale`), `admin` (role `Admin`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "gatewayBaseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5100" },
    { "key": "notificationsBaseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5104" },
    { "key": "orderingBaseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5102" },
    { "key": "flowSku", "value": "GOLDEN-LAGER-350" },
    { "key": "shortSku", "value": "MIDNIGHT-STOUT-500" },
    { "key": "orderId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "rejectedOrderId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "pollAttempts", "value": "0" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "otherToken", "value": "" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Shared helper: every non-2xx response must be a ProblemDetails body with a trace id.",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "    pm.test('Error is RFC 9457 ProblemDetails with traceId', () => {",
          "        pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/problem+json');",
          "        const problem = pm.response.json();",
          "        pm.expect(problem.status).to.eql(pm.response.code);",
          "        pm.expect(problem).to.have.property('traceId');",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Sign in",
      "description": "Tokens come from the Gateway; the Function validates them itself, in a worker middleware.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get point of sale token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const token = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Role is PointOfSale', () => pm.expect(token.role).to.eql('PointOfSale'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', token.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"bar\",\n  \"password\": \"demo\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/auth/token",
              "host": ["{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Places the orders of the end-to-end folder and reads its own notifications."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get another point of sale token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const token = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('It is a different point of sale', () => pm.expect(token.username).to.eql('market'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('otherToken', token.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"market\",\n  \"password\": \"demo\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/auth/token",
              "host": ["{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Used to show that the panel is scoped to the caller."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Notifications - queries",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get notifications",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const notifications = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('The panel is a list', () => pm.expect(notifications).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('Rows are newest first', () => {",
                  "    const created = notifications.map(n => n.createdOnUtc);",
                  "    pm.expect(created).to.eql([...created].sort().reverse());",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Every row says what happened and what the e-mail did', () => {",
                  "    notifications.forEach(n => {",
                  "        pm.expect(['OrderConfirmed', 'OrderRejected']).to.include(n.type);",
                  "        pm.expect(['Pending', 'Skipped', 'Sent', 'Failed']).to.include(n.emailStatus);",
                  "        pm.expect(n.title).to.be.a('string').and.not.be.empty;",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/notifications",
              "host": ["{{notificationsBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "notifications"]
            },
            "description": "The caller's notifications, newest first (at most 100). The caller is the `sub` claim of the token: there is no endpoint that takes a customer id, so one point of sale cannot ask for another one's panel."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get notifications - through the Gateway",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('The Gateway route answers the same thing as the Function', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/notifications",
              "host": ["{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "notifications"]
            },
            "description": "The same request through YARP. The route is GET only: the panel is read-only, so a write method is refused by the Gateway before it reaches the Function."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get notifications - without a token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('The Function refuses it itself', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('Notifications.Unauthenticated');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/notifications",
              "host": ["{{notificationsBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "notifications"]
            },
            "description": "Called directly, without the Gateway in front: the Function validates the token in a worker middleware, so being inside the cluster is not a credential."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get notifications - with a token signed by somebody else",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJiYXIiLCJlbWFpbCI6ImJhckBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInJvbGUiOiJQb2ludE9mU2FsZSIsImlzcyI6Im1pY3Jvc2VydmljZXMtZGVtbyIsImF1ZCI6Im1pY3Jvc2VydmljZXMtZGVtby1hcGkiLCJleHAiOjQxMDI0NDQ4MDB9.zqCJmtGgKDJGH9xhMC1QxVMhZLh0cUmZVkkYVAEIBOA",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/notifications",
              "host": ["{{notificationsBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "notifications"]
            },
            "description": "A well-formed token with the right claims but the wrong signing key. The signature is what makes a token trustworthy, not its shape."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Order flow (end to end)",
      "description": "Places an order and waits for its notification. Between the two there are three broker hops and two other services.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Place an order within stock",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const order = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('The order starts Pending', () => pm.expect(order.status).to.eql('Pending'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('orderId', order.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('pollAttempts', 0);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"sku\": \"{{flowSku}}\", \"quantity\": 2 }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{orderingBaseUrl}}/api/orders",
              "host": ["{{orderingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "Ordering answers 202 immediately; everything after this happens through events."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Notification of the confirmed order arrives",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Three broker hops plus an SMTP send, so give it a moment between attempts.",
                  "// setTimeout is how a Postman script sleeps: the sandbox waits for pending timers before sending.",
                  "setTimeout(() => {}, 1000);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const orderId = pm.collectionVariables.get('orderId');",
                  "const notification = pm.response.json().find(n => n.orderId === orderId);",
                  "const attempts = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('pollAttempts')) + 1;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('pollAttempts', attempts);",
                  "",
                  "if (!notification && attempts < 20) {",
                  "    pm.execution.setNextRequest('Notification of the confirmed order arrives');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    pm.test(`The notification arrived after ${attempts} attempt(s)`, () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(notification, 'notification for the order').to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "        pm.expect(notification.type).to.eql('OrderConfirmed');",
                  "        pm.expect(notification.title).to.include('confirmed');",
                  "        pm.expect(notification.body).to.include(orderId);",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('It is the newest row in the panel', () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(pm.response.json()[0].orderId).to.eql(orderId);",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('The e-mail was attempted (read it in Mailpit on http://localhost:8025)', () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(['Pending', 'Skipped', 'Sent', 'Failed']).to.include(notification.emailStatus);",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('pollAttempts', 0);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/notifications",
              "host": ["{{notificationsBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "notifications"]
            },
            "description": "Polls the panel until the Function has consumed `OrderConfirmed`. The whole chain is: OrderPlaced → reservation → StockReserved → OrderConfirmed → notification + e-mail."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Another point of sale does not see it",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const orderId = pm.collectionVariables.get('orderId');",
                  "pm.test('The order just notified to bar is absent from market\\'s panel', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().map(n => n.orderId)).to.not.include(orderId);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{otherToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/notifications",
              "host": ["{{notificationsBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "notifications"]
            },
            "description": "Same endpoint, different token. The query is scoped to the `sub` claim, so the notification that just arrived for `bar` is simply not in `market`'s panel."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Place an order that cannot be fulfilled",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const order = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('A rejection is not an HTTP error: the order is accepted first', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(order.status).to.eql('Pending');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('rejectedOrderId', order.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('pollAttempts', 0);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"sku\": \"{{shortSku}}\", \"quantity\": 900 }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{orderingBaseUrl}}/api/orders",
              "host": ["{{orderingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "900 packs of the deliberately short SKU: more than the warehouse could ever hold, so the run stays repeatable."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Notification of the rejected order arrives",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "setTimeout(() => {}, 1000);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const orderId = pm.collectionVariables.get('rejectedOrderId');",
                  "const notification = pm.response.json().find(n => n.orderId === orderId);",
                  "const attempts = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('pollAttempts')) + 1;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('pollAttempts', attempts);",
                  "",
                  "if (!notification && attempts < 20) {",
                  "    pm.execution.setNextRequest('Notification of the rejected order arrives');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    pm.test(`The rejection was notified after ${attempts} attempt(s)`, () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(notification, 'notification for the rejected order').to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "        pm.expect(notification.type).to.eql('OrderRejected');",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('The customer is told why, and that nothing was reserved', () => {",
                  "        pm.expect(notification.body).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('shortSku'));",
                  "        pm.expect(notification.body).to.include('Nothing was reserved');",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/notifications",
              "host": ["{{notificationsBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "notifications"]
            },
            "description": "The compensation path is notified exactly like the happy one: the customer learns the outcome either way."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  }
}
